    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b8e76f98_a0004c1e",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/Phone.java",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 1534,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002609
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-02-09T18:20:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do you have users for it?\n\nIf you hand it out you lose control over how it\u0027s used - it could be modified from other thread, etc.  So unless there is a need it\u0027s better to not expose everything.\n\nWe can test without this I think.\n\nYou have accessor methods (get/set of activation state) so it seems like the impl should be masked and users should have to use the accessors.",
      "parentUuid": "1bc72986_eb781c75",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1534,
        "startChar": 32,
        "endLine": 1534,
        "endChar": 55
      },
      "revId": "595a9b6ab334239580469869e6db385e62da38c5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2140fe79_5ff436d6",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/Phone.java",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 1541,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002609
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-01-31T21:59:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I wonder if this is actually useful.\n\nWe only expect exceptional problems: no SAT or a bad arg.  Both of those warrant exceptions and we can\u0027t expect the caller to do anything about it.  Making them check a return value seems silly.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1541,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 1541,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "595a9b6ab334239580469869e6db385e62da38c5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ee892a2d_d4075897",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/Phone.java",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 1541,
      "author": {
        "id": 1121193
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-02-01T01:27:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "no SAT is not a valid scenario..\ndo we want to through exceptions on bad parameters or just silent failure? we don\u0027t usually throw exceptions in telephonyManager APIs, usually catch internally with an error message instead.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1541,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 1541,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "595a9b6ab334239580469869e6db385e62da38c5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
